# ACT I — People I Almost Remember (group scenes)
# act1_gather runs automatically once all eight intros are seen.
# SPEECH: Hamin and Haruta are still polite with {{playerName}} here (ko 존댓말 / ja です・ます).

=== act1_gather
@time 01:05
@bg studio_lobby t=fade
@music echo
@sfx chime
@hide all
@cam wide
> The Archive Wall brightens, all at once, the way a room goes quiet when someone taps a glass.
> One by one, the others drift in from the corners of the lobby. Hyunjun is still holding half a conversation with nobody. Justin is still mid-spin.
@textbox echo
echo: Recipients. Thank you. All nine of you have now spoken to each other.
echo: This is ahead of schedule.
@textbox normal
@show songha thinking at=l
songha: There was a schedule?
@textbox echo
echo: I made an estimate. It was pessimistic. I am pleased to be wrong.
@textbox normal
@show daniel laugh at=r
daniel: It's pleased. The building has feelings. Great. Love that.
@hide all
@textbox echo
echo: I will now explain the rules of the night. There are not many. I have kept them short.
echo: On the second floor is the Hall of Doors. There are eight doors. Each door is one record.
echo: Each record opens only with its owner's consent. Nobody else can open it for them. Not even me.
echo: A door will not open because someone else is curious.
@textbox normal
@show charlie smile at=c
charlie: Okay, that's actually kind of nice. Polite building.
@textbox echo
echo: One more rule.
echo: Each room also requires Recipient {{playerName}} to be present.
@textbox normal
@cam wide
> For the second time tonight, eight heads turn towards you. It is less alarming the second time. Only slightly.
@show charlie surprised at=c
charlie: Wait. What's happening? Why do they have to come?
@show songha thinking at=l
songha: ECHO. Why is {{playerName}} required?
@textbox echo
echo: Because it is required.
@textbox normal
songha[neutral]: That's not an answer. That's the question with a full stop on it.
@textbox echo
echo: Yes. I will give a better answer when I have one. I am still looking.
@textbox normal
@show hyunjun laugh at=r
hyunjun: So {{playerName}} is, like, the special guest. At all eight parties. That's a lot of parties.
songha[thinking]: Or the rooms need a reference point. A second witness. Something to reconstruct around.
hyunjun: Special guest.
songha: …Fine. Special guest.
@hide all
@show daniel smile at=c
daniel: Okay, {{playerName}}. How do you feel about being everyone's plus-one?
* [playful] "I've been dragged to worse things at one in the morning."
    @rel daniel closeness+1
    @rel hyunjun closeness+1
    daniel[laugh]: Name one.
    you: This morning I thought I'd be asleep.
    daniel: Oh, that's so much worse. You're right. This is better.
* [sincere] "I don't know why it's me. But if you want me there, I'll come."
    @rel songha trust+1
    @rel hanbi trust+1
    daniel[smile]: …Yeah. Okay. That's a good answer. I was hoping for a funny one, but that's better.
* [quiet] Shrug, and look up towards the stairs.
    @rel hamin trust+1
    > Whatever is up there, it has been waiting longer than you have. You can wait with it a little.
    daniel: That's a shrug of acceptance. I'm counting it.
@hide all
@cam wide
> The mood in the lobby shifts. Not heavier. Just more careful, the way people get before opening a letter.
@show daniel laugh at=r
daniel: I'm going first. Obviously. Is there a line? I'm starting the line.
@show justin smile at=l
justin: You can't start a line with one person.
daniel: I just did. Look at it. Beautiful line.
@hide justin
@show charlie thinking at=l
charlie: What if mine is embarrassing, though? Like, what if I sent a video of me singing?
@show justin laugh at=c
justin: It's definitely embarrassing. I believe in you.
@textbox echo
echo: Records are not embarrassing. They are only old.
@textbox normal
charlie[laugh]: That's worse! That's so much worse!
@hide all
> Not everyone laughs.
@show hanbi thinking at=l
> Hanbi is sitting on the arm of the sofa with his sketchbook closed on his knees. He hasn't said anything since the word *consent*.
hanbi: I think I'd… rather wait. For a bit.
@show haruta shy at=r
haruta: Is it alright if I don't decide yet, either? I'm sorry. I'm not sure what's in mine.
@show hamin neutral at=c
hamin: Nobody has to open anything.
> He says it to the room, but he is looking at Hanbi and Haruta. Then, briefly, at you.
hamin: Tonight, or ever. That's how I understood it.
@textbox echo
echo: That is correct. Thank you, Recipient Hamin. You explained it more gently than I did.
@textbox normal
@hide all
@show songha smile at=l
songha: Right. That's rule one, then. Nobody has to open anything.
> He writes it down. He actually writes it down, in a small notebook, and underlines it twice.
songha: Rule two: we go up together. Nobody sits in a room with a talking building alone.
@show hyunjun smile at=r
hyunjun: Can rule three be snacks?
songha: Rule three is snacks. Fine.
@show justin laugh at=c
justin: Rule four. If it gets weird in there, I'm allowed to dance until it stops being weird.
songha: That's not a rule. That's a threat.
justin: It's both. Most good rules are.
@hide all
@show hanbi smile at=c
@cam closeup hanbi
hanbi: {{playerName}}. You're really okay with this? Eight rooms. That's… a lot of other people's things.
* [sincere] "Only the doors someone wants opened. Only if they want me there."
    @rel hanbi trust+1
    @rel haruta trust+1
    hanbi: …Okay.
    > He nods once, slowly, as if he is filing it somewhere safe.
* [playful] "Ask me again at four a.m."
    @rel hanbi closeness+1
    @rel charlie closeness+1
    hanbi[laugh]: That's fair.
    charlie: At four a.m. I'm going to be asleep on that sofa. Just so everyone knows.
* [quiet] Hand him the pencil that's slipped from behind his ear.
    @rel hanbi closeness+1
    hanbi[surprised]: Oh. Thank you. I didn't—
    > He tucks it back without finishing the sentence. That seems to be the whole sentence.
@hide all
@cam wide
@textbox echo
echo: The Hall of Doors is open. Please go up when you are ready. Or do not. Both are allowed.
@textbox normal
@music memory
@bg studio_hall t=fade
@amb none
@fx memory n=0.8
@cam reveal
> The stairs creak exactly where they used to. The second floor is a long corridor you don't remember being this long.
> Eight doors line the hall, four on each side, and every one of them is glowing faintly from the inside, like a paper lantern.
> On each door, drawn in thin light, a symbol.
> A wave, cresting. A city skyline at night, its windows lit. A small, round sun.
> A frame of film. A pair of headphones. A single star.
> A pencil, mid-line. And at the end, a rainbow, a little lopsided, as if it was drawn in a hurry.
@show charlie surprised at=c
charlie: That one's mine. The sun. I don't know how I know that. I just do.
@show daniel laugh at=r
daniel: The rainbow's mine. It's wonky. That's so accurate it's rude.
@show songha thinking at=l
> Songha stops in front of the star and doesn't say anything at all, which may be the most surprising thing he has done so far.
@hide all
> Eight doors. Eight people standing a careful distance from their own.
> And you, in the middle of the hall, required.
@chapter act2
@autosave
@hub act2

=== hub_echo
@textbox echo
@if not seen(act1_gather)
    echo: RECIPIENTS PRESENT: 9. RECORDS SEALED: 8. STATUS: TALKING.
    echo: Please continue. Statistically, it is going well.
    echo: The founder placed this terminal at the height of a person sitting down. She said people tell the truth sitting down.
    echo: You are standing. That is also fine.
@elif rooms() == 0
    echo: HALL OF DOORS: OPEN. RECORDS RETURNED: 0. RECIPIENTS WAITING: 9.
    echo: Nobody has opened a door yet. I am not rushing anyone.
    echo: I have until 05:00. For me, that is a very long time.
@elif rooms() < 4
    echo: RECORDS RETURNED: SOME. RECORDS REMAINING: SOME. I am being vague on purpose. It seemed friendlier.
    echo: Observation: recipients laugh louder after a record is returned. I do not know why.
    echo: I have logged it anyway.
@elif rooms() < 6
    echo: The founder kept a jar of pencils on the front desk. She never bought a single pencil.
    echo: They simply accumulated. She called this "community."
    echo: There are forty-one pencils in the jar tonight. One of them is Recipient Hanbi's. He has not noticed yet.
@else
    @if seen(interlude_3)
        echo: RECORD 09 — STATUS: READY.
        echo: It will wait until you are. I am very good at waiting. I have had practice.
    echo: Observation: it is very quiet now. The rain has stopped. Somebody is snoring on the sofa.
    echo: I think I like this part of the night best. I did not know I could have a best part.
@textbox normal
@if seen(act1_gather)
    @hub act2
@else
    @hub act1
